  "executive_summary": "Agent host capacity is driven by tool execution costs, not model inference. Field data shows that each workflow's expense aligns with the cumulative tool work performed by agents, making tool throughput the primary scaling factor. A recommendation is to provision hosts based on projected tool call volume, targeting 80% CPU utilization and 70% memory headroom, while monitoring tool latency to adjust capacity dynamically.",
